<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0005">Example <span data-tag="0005">11.5.0.68</span> <span class="named">(Singular Homology)</span>.</a> For any topological space $X$, the <em>singular homology groups</em> $\operatorname{ \mathrm{H} }_{\ast }(X; \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}})$ are defined as the homology groups of a chain complex </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \cdots \xrightarrow {\partial } \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ \operatorname{Sing}_{2}(X) ] \xrightarrow { \partial } \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ \operatorname{Sing}_1(X) ] \xrightarrow {\partial } \operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ \operatorname{Sing}_0(X) ], \]
</div>
<p> where $\operatorname{\mathbf{Z}}[ \operatorname{Sing}_ n(X) ]$ denotes the free abelian group generated by the set $\operatorname{Sing}_ n(X)$ and the differential is given on generators by the formula </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \partial (\sigma ) = \sum _{i = 0}^{n} (-1)^{i} d^{n}_ i \sigma . \]
</div>
</article>
